<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lars Tolumnius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 437 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lars Tolumnius was king of the Etruscan city of Veii in the late 5th century BCE. Roman tradition says he incited the Roman colony of Fidenae to revolt and had Roman envoys killed, and that he was slain in single combat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aulus-cornelius-cossus">Aulus Cornelius Cossus</a>, who dedicated his armour as the spolia opima. The war over Fidenae was part of Veii's long rivalry with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lars-tolumnius.jpg" alt="Lars Tolumnius" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Etruskischer_Meister_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
